{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative exploration supervisor: random_walk is used for coverage in clear, safe states; move_forward is used only in a short forward_commit state. Obstacle events always force a transition to a dedicated recovery state, which enables only a single, safe turn (rotate_clockwise for front/left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles). Full_rotate is reserved for the rare case of repeated front obstacles. Recovery states return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. All transitions are deterministic and safe.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception; all motion commands are open-loop pulses.",
    "Supervisor specification ensures: (1) random_walk is the default in clear/search states, (2) move_forward is only used in a short commit state, (3) obstacle events always force a one-shot recovery turn, (4) recovery states enable only a single, safe controllable, (5) full_rotate is used only after repeated front obstacles, (6) transitions are deterministic and total for uncontrollables."
  ],
